  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The first step in finding the product \\((3x+2)(x-5)\\) by use of the distributive property in the form \\(a(b+c)=ab+ac\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(3x^2-13x-10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(3x(x-5)+2(x-5)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\((3x+2)x+(3x+2)(-5)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(3x^2-17x-10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(3x^2+2x-15x-10\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1957-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Using the property in precisely the stated form, set \\(a=3x+2,\\) \\(b=x,\\) and \\(c=-5.\\) Then \\[ \\begin{gathered} (3x+2)(x-5)\\\\ =(3x+2)x+(3x+2)(-5). \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Match the second factor with \\(b+c\\) in the stated form",
        "Take \\(a=3x+2,\\) \\(b=x,\\) and \\(c=-5\\)"
      ],
